+//
+// `TZ` set to `:America/Sao_Paulo`. POSIX leaves what follows a leading `:`
+// to the implementation, and H-13.1 strips the `:` and reads the rest as a
+// name, as the GNU C library does (`meta/research/tz-environment.md`): the
+// name is `America/Sao_Paulo`, and a step 1 that kept the `:` reads
+// `:America/Sao_Paulo`.
+//
+// ON ANY MACHINE: `TZ` is step 1, so it answers before `/etc/localtime` and
+// `/etc/timezone` are read -- and on every machine this suite runs on, CI's
+// included, `/etc/localtime` is a link that WOULD answer, so a discovery that
